    {
      "#": 1,
      "status": "confirmed",
      "protected_subject": "authorization-authentication",
      "reason": "Precondition is a verify=True request with cert= followed by any later verify=True request in the process; my rerun of tmp/leak/demo.py at HEAD 4089f3dc (urllib3 2.8.0) showed server B receiving commonName=alice-client from a cert-less second Session, because adapters.py:95 shares one context and urllib3 ssl_.py:431 calls load_cert_chain on it; real-world incidence (mTLS users combining verify=True with cert=) was not measured."
